
######## Monday, the 20th of July, 1931 (raining (10° to 16°C)) ########
   ◆ Ada's past: "He has been a good son to me, and I have tried to do my duty by him."
   ◆ Arthur's past: He was never known to spend more than he could afford.
   ◆ Mr. Thomas's past: He was always scrupulously punctual in his payments, and never owed a farthing in his life.
   📅 Ada means to: Tuesday: washes up the crockery, sets the place to rights, and tidies Bert | Wednesday: cleans the boots and knives and forks, and goes out to do shopping | Thursday: darns socks, and looks over Bert's clothes | Friday: washes the linen and does the family mending | Saturday: makes the beds, and sweeps and polishes the rooms
   📅 Arthur means to: Monday: posts his letters | Tuesday: goes to the City and collects his rents | Wednesday: sees about getting his life insured | Thursday: pays the premium and takes the receipt | Friday: deposits the money in the savings bank
   📅 Mr. Thomas means to: Tuesday: sees to the blinds | Wednesday: pays the milkman | Thursday: goes to the doctor about his leg | Friday: pays the charwoman
